          <button class="btn mark" aria-pressed="false">Mark done</button>
        </div>
        <div class="step-body" id="body-2" hidden>
          <p>Two paths, depending on whether you still have last week’s chat.</p>
          <p><strong>If you still have the chat:</strong> scroll to the code the AI gave you. Skip ahead to <em>Run it</em>.</p>
          <p><strong>If you don’t:</strong> start a new chat and describe the generator again, in your own words. Your prompt should say:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>What goes in</strong> - some text: a web address, a message, anything</li>
            <li><strong>What comes out</strong> - a QR code for it, shown on the page</li>
            <li>That there’s a button to save the code as a picture</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Then paste this specification at the end. It tells the AI how to build things for this course; you’ll understand what each line means later in this course.</p>
          <div class="prompt">
            <button class="btn copy" data-copy="spec-block">Copy specification</button>
            <pre id="spec-block">Build it to this specification:

          # SPECIFICATIONS

          * Everything in one single HTML file - HTML, CSS, and JavaScript together
          * No build tools - no React, Vue, or anything requiring npm
          * CDN libraries are fine if they help
          * Use vanilla JavaScript only
          * Fully responsive - works on phone, tablet, and desktop
          * Fully accessible - semantic HTML, ARIA labels, keyboard navigation
          * No data sent to any server - everything runs in the browser only
          * Versioning in comments (e.g., // v1.0 - initial build)
          * Very descriptive JavaScript comments explaining each code block in plain language</pre>
          </div>
          <p class="aside">Keep the prompt to the plain generator for now. Your color and your initials come in steps 4 and 5.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <!-- ============ 3 - RUN IT ============ -->
